    {
      "title": "map, filter, reduce and Laziness",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "map, filter, reduce and Laziness",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. map, filter, flatMap, reduce",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Op",
                "Takes",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`map`",
                  "Function",
                  "1:1 transform"
                ],
                [
                  "`filter`",
                  "Predicate",
                  "keeps true ones"
                ],
                [
                  "`flatMap`",
                  "Function to Stream",
                  "1:N, `List<List<T>>` to `Stream<T>`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`reduce(identity, op)` returns ==T==",
                "`reduce(op)` returns ==Optional<T>==",
                "Op must be **associative**, identity **neutral** (parallel-safe)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Laziness",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Intermediate ops run nothing until a ==terminal op==",
                "No terminal op: `peek`/`map` prints never fire",
                "Elements flow ==one at a time== through all stages",
                "`findFirst`, `anyMatch`, `limit` stop early, even on infinite streams"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "Stream.of(1, 2)",
                ".peek(n -> print(\"a\" + n))",
                ".map(n -> n * 2)",
                ".peek(n -> print(\"b\" + n))",
                ".toList();"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "a1",
                "b2",
                "a2",
                "b4"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Primitives and Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`mapToInt(...).sum()/average()/max()` avoid boxing",
                "`boxed()` converts back to `Stream<Integer>`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Filter and map print nothing?** No terminal op, so nothing runs",
                "**Two peeks, what order?** Interleaved per element",
                "**map vs flatMap?** 1:1 versus flatten 1:N",
                "**reduce vs collect?** Immutable fold versus mutable container"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Collectors: groupingBy, toMap and More",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Collectors: groupingBy, toMap and More",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Collect to a Container",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`collect(Collectors.toList()/toSet())` = ==mutable reduction==",
                "Stream `toList()` (16+) is **unmodifiable**",
                "`joining(\", \", \"[\", \"]\")` builds a ==String==: `[a, b, c]`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. groupingBy vs partitioningBy",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`groupingBy(classifier)` → `Map<K, List<T>>`",
                "A ==downstream== collector changes the value",
                "Default map is an unordered `HashMap`: ==don't rely on order=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Collector",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`groupingBy(Emp::dept, counting())`",
                  "count per dept"
                ],
                [
                  "`groupingBy(Emp::dept, summingInt(Emp::pay))`",
                  "sum per dept"
                ],
                [
                  "`groupingBy(Emp::dept, mapping(Emp::name, toList()))`",
                  "names per dept"
                ],
                [
                  "`groupingBy(Emp::dept, averagingDouble(Emp::pay))`",
                  "average per dept"
                ],
                [
                  "`partitioningBy(pred)`",
                  "`Map<Boolean, List<T>>`, ==true and false== keys always present"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 4
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "Map<String, Long> n = emps.stream().collect(",
                "  Collectors.groupingBy(Emp::dept,",
                "    TreeMap::new, Collectors.counting()));"
              ],
              "note": "middle argument sets the map type"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. toMap Pitfalls",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`toMap(keyFn, valueFn)` + duplicate key → {red:IllegalStateException}",
                "Fix: merge function `toMap(k, v, (a, b) -> a)`",
                "A ==null value== throws {red:NPE}",
                "4th arg picks the map: `toMap(k, v, merge, TreeMap::new)`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Count per group: `groupingBy(f, counting())`. Map of sums: `groupingBy(f, summingInt(g))`. Yes/no split: `partitioningBy`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Optional and Common Stream Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Optional and Common Stream Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Optional: Create and Consume",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Optional<T>== = empty or one value; a **return type** for 'maybe no result'",
                "`of(x)` {red:NPE} on null; `ofNullable(x)`; `empty()`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Behaviour"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`orElse(d)`",
                  "==eager==: d built always"
                ],
                [
                  "`orElseGet(s)`",
                  "==lazy==: only if empty"
                ],
                [
                  "`orElseThrow()`",
                  "throws if empty"
                ],
                [
                  "`ifPresent(c)`",
                  "run if present"
                ],
                [
                  "`ifPresentOrElse(c, r)`",
                  "both branches"
                ],
                [
                  "`map` `flatMap` `filter`",
                  "chain, no null checks"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "String n = Optional.ofNullable(user)",
                "    .map(User::name)",
                "    .orElseGet(() -> \"guest\");"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Optional Don'ts",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`get()` without `isPresent()`",
                "Optional as field, parameter or collection",
                "Returning `null` from an Optional method"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Stream Mistakes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Reuse: {red:IllegalStateException} stream has already been operated upon or closed",
                "Fix: ==new stream per use==",
                "Mutating outside state in `map`/`forEach`: unsafe in parallel",
                "Modifying source mid-pipeline: ConcurrentModificationException",
                "`parallel()` on small or I/O-bound work",
                "`peek` for logic: debug only"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**orElse vs orElseGet?** Eager vs lazy argument",
                "**Optional field or parameter?** Not serializable; null still possible",
                "**Stream reuse?** One-shot view; terminal op closes it"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
